Task: Harden Parliament video Conductor implementation plans

Summary:
- Expanded all six active Parliament video Conductor tracks with detailed implementation discipline.
- Added fallback-resource coverage for TVNZ Archive, Ngā Taonga Sound & Vision, RNZ, Parliament Today/AM Network, Archives New Zealand, Internet Archive, and web archives.
- Added explicit per-task commit/git notes requirements, phase checkpoint requirements, push-after-phase requirements, and GitHub Actions failure repair requirements.
- Added github_actions metadata to each video track.
- Added scripts/check_parliament_video_track_plan.py and tests/test_parliament_video_track_plan.py.
- Wired the checker into pixi.toml and .github/workflows/quality.yml.

Validation:
- pixi run parliament-video-track-plan
- pixi run python -m pytest -q tests/test_parliament_video_track_plan.py
- pixi run lint scripts/check_parliament_video_track_plan.py tests/test_parliament_video_track_plan.py
- pixi run format-check
- pixi run workflow-audit
- pixi run toml-check

Why:
The video archive programme needs an auditable metadata-first plan that is enforced by CI before implementation begins. This commit makes the Conductor tracks and GitHub Actions agree on that discipline.
